<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Dos Bocas crude port says it reopens.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Dos Bocas crude port says it reopens.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's three main crude ports were all operating early Thursday as Dos Bocas reopened Wednesday at 2200 local/0300 GMT after a storm in the Gulf of Mexico waned, port officials said.</p>
<p>The port originally closed Wednesday at 1245. Pajaritos port also shut to crude exports for about six hours, while Cayo Arcas port remained open during the storms.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
</text>
